 "title": "Complexity: count the steps as n grows",
 "kind": "structure",
 "intro": "Big-O is just step counting. We will count a plain loop, a nested loop and a halving loop for n = 8.",
 "predict": {
  "question": "If n doubles from 8 to 16, how many steps does the nested loop run?",
  "options": [
   "128",
   "256",
   "32"
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "reveal": "256. The nested loop does n x n steps, so doubling n makes it 4 times bigger: 8 x 8 = 64 becomes 16 x 16 = 256."
 },
